DOCKER FILE;
A simple plain text containing instructions to build a docker image

We can scan the docker image using Docker scout, or trivy, integrated into the docker desktop OR Docker CLI

DOCKER IMAGE: 
is a package that contains everything an application needs to run including the application code, dependencies, lib, software, instruction etc.

DOCKER CONTAINER:
Its the instance runtime of a docker image

DOCKER BEST PRACTICES:
1) Using the official docker image as our base image in our docker file
2) Reduce the number of run commands so as to reduce the number of layers in the image inorder to keep the image light weight
3)Scan the image before using
4)Use executable over shell form for commands so that our applictaion will run as a parent process & wont be killed unnoticed.


